# Me API — contexto del usuario autenticado (REST Client)
#
# Requisitos:
#   1. API en marcha → pnpm --filter api run dev
#   2. Login en auth.http o abajo → @accessToken
#   3. GET/PATCH /me requieren empresa en el JWT (@RequireCompany)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@email = prueba@ejemplo.com
@password = Password123
@branchId = reemplazar-con-id-de-sucursal

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

###

@accessToken = {{login.response.body.$.data.accessToken}}

### Mi perfil (usuario + membership en empresa activa)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### Mi empresa (única membership)
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/company
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### Mi sucursal por defecto
GET {{baseUrl}}/me/branch
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### Actualizar mi perfil
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Javier",
  "lastName": "Actualizado"
}

###

### Cambiar mi contraseña (revoca todas las sesiones refresh)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/me/password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "{{password}}",
  "newPassword": "NuevaPassword123"
}

###

### Cambiar sucursal por defecto
POST {{baseUrl}}/me/switch-branch
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "branchId": "{{branchId}}"
}
